.TH CDCSTORE-ADD 1 "October 2026" "cdcstore" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cdcstore\-add \- store files in a cdcstore repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cdcstore\-add
\-d DEST [options] SOURCE...
.br
.B cdcstore\-add
\-X [options] DIR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stores files in a cdcstore repository: each file is cut into content\-defined chunks (a file up to \-s bytes is a single chunk) and every chunk is written as its own file. Nothing is deduplicated, compressed or packed here; that is the job of the sorter and the archiver, which take the chunk list from cdcstore\-list \-k.
.PP
A SOURCE is a directory (scanned recursively), a file, or \- for a list of paths on standard input, stored in the order given. Nothing is sorted here, so any sorter fits. Paths are stored without a leading / or ./ and may not contain ... Adding to an existing repository keeps that repository's \-a and \-s.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d DEST
Store into the repository DEST (made if it is new). The originals stay where they are.
.TP
.B \-X
In place: DIR becomes the repository (DIR/.cdcstore). The originals in DIR are DELETED once they are stored and a full check has passed. A notice is printed, and you are asked first unless \-y is given.
.TP
.B \-a N
Average chunk size for files above \-s (default 16384; rounded to a power of two between 1 KiB and 4 MiB). Only matters for a new repository.
.TP
.B \-s N
Files up to N bytes are stored whole, as one chunk (default 65536). Only matters for a new repository.
.TP
.B \-C DIR
Store paths relative to DIR, like tar \-C. A path that is not under DIR is an error.
.TP
.B \-y
With \-X: do not ask before deleting (the DANGER notice is still printed).
.TP
.B \-S
Skip the final sync of the disk. Faster, but after a power cut cdcstore\-verify can find missing chunk files.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet.
.TP
.B \-h
Print help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
cdcstore\-add \-d REPO /path/to/files
find /path/to/files \-type f | sortof\-natural \- | cdcstore\-add \-d REPO \-
.RE
.fi
.sp
